        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "Calling a generator function runs none of its body. It just returns a generator object. The first next runs the body until the first yield, hands out that value, and freezes every local variable in place. The second call resumes on the line after the yield, loops, and yields again. When the body finishes, the generator raises stop iteration, and a for loop simply ends.",
